# ~/.config/xdg-terminals.list — which terminal is "the" terminal.
#
# Read by xdg-terminal-exec, which is what any "open in terminal" action goes
# through: the picker scripts, file managers, and desktop entries that declare
# Terminal=true. Listed in order of preference; the first one installed wins.
#
# foot is listed second because it is what the picker windows use — they pass
# their own --app-id explicitly, so this list does not affect them.

ghostty.desktop
foot.desktop
